    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Why do youth receive technical violations?\"\nformat: html\n---\n\n\n**Why do youth receive technical violations?** \n\n* What are the most common reasons for technical violations when the violation was the primary offense? How do reasons vary across race/ethnicity, sex, and risk level? \n\n* What are the most common offenses when the violation was not the primary offense? \n\n\n\n**Double check following coding/grouping of technical violations with team:**\n\n* \"100a  Violation Probation - General\" = \"General Violation\"\n\n* \"5100c  Viol Prob - Discharge Unsatisfactorily From Placement (2)\",\"5100j  Viol Prob - Violating Placement Rules (3)\" = \"Violation Related to Placement\"\n\n* \"5100d  Viol Prob - Runaway From Home/Placement\" = \"Runaway\",\n\n* \"5100e  Viol Prob - Failure to Report to Probation Officer (2)\" = \"Failure to Report to PO\",\n\n* \"5100i - Viol Prob - Violating School Rules\" = \"Violation of School Rules\",\n\n* \"5100f  Viol Prob - Curfew Violation (3)\" = \"Curfew Violation\",\n\n* \"5100l Viol Prob - Failure to Participate in Order Program (11)\" = \"Failure to Participate in Program\",\n\n* \"5100h  Viol Prob - Truancy - Not attending each Class each Day (4)\",\"5103c  Truancy 3 Days\" = \"Curfew Violation\",\n\n* \"5100b  Absenting Self From Court Order Placement (2,6)\",\"5100g  Viol Prob - Failure to Notify PO Of change Of Home/School/Employment Address (5)\",\"5100k  Viol Prob - Failure to Pay Probation Fees (9)\",\"xxx - Converted Data\") = \"Other\",\n\n* \"No Violation/Modification Needed\" = \"No Violation\" (*I have filtered these out from the first section*)\n\n<br>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n# 1. Most Common Reasons for Technical Violations\n\n<br>\n\n## Table 1. By FY: Most Common Reasons for Technical Violations\n\n**NOTE:** The base sample and denominator for this analysis is all filed violations where the most serious violation was a technical violation.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output